// presets that give session variety without pretending to be real-time.
//
// Per Rick's requirements meeting: each scenario carries its own base supply
// and base demand (host-editable), plus one scenario-specific field:
//   Stable Market   - supply + demand only
//   Rising Costs    - supply + demand + a cost increase per week
//   Supply Shock    - supply + demand + a reference price + an impact level (Low/Mid/High)
//   Efficient Chain - supply + demand + a price reduction per week
// Starting price is intentionally NOT one of these fields - it stays a
// separate, standalone setting elsewhere on the setup screen.
// ---------- NEWS SYSTEM: Global & Local ----------
// Curated, not live. A static classroom file has no safe way to pull a real
// news feed: no content moderation on what shows up, another exposed API
// key, another quota that can run out mid-session. So this is a fixed,
// hand-written pool (10 global, 30 local) that the Facilitator picks from
// directly, with zero external dependency.
//
// Global news is chain-wide: it temporarily adjusts holding/stockout cost
